    role: "Bowler", era: "Modern Legend",    bio: "Shane Keith Warne was born in Melbourne, Victoria. As a child, he dreamed of playing Australian Rules Football for St Kilda. A broken leg ended his football aspirations, and he turned to cricket. He made his Test debut in 1992 and took his first wicket on his 22nd birthday.\n\nWarne revolutionized leg-spin bowling, a dying art in the early 1990s. His first ball in Ashes cricket \u2014 the 'Ball of the Century' in 1993 \u2014 drifted wide outside leg stump, pitched on middle, and clipped Mike Gatting's off bail. It is the most replayed delivery in cricket history. Warne took 708 Test wickets, the most by any spin bowler at the time of his retirement.\n\nBeyond the numbers, Warne was cricket's greatest showman. His battles with Sachin Tendulkar defined an era. He revived leg-spin as an art form, inspiring spinners worldwide. Off the field, his life was colorful and controversial, but his cricketing genius was never in doubt. He died suddenly in 2022 at age 52, shocking the cricket world.",
